This repository is published to be READ, not reused. It is a portfolio piece:
the reasoning is the point, and hiding the source would hide the evidence.

Two parts are carved out and carry their own terms. They are listed at the
bottom, and nothing in this file narrows them.

────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
YOU MAY

  · View, read, clone and study any part of this repository.
  · Quote short excerpts in commentary, review, teaching or criticism, with
    attribution to David Reyburn and a link to the source.
  · Link to it, and cite the measurements it publishes.
  · Consume the machine-readable manifests — custom-elements.json and
    verdigris/fonts/manifest.json — in an editor, language server or other
    developer tool. They are published so tooling can read them, and that
    would be a hollow offer if reading them were a breach.

